    "gloss": "How I wish there were a single life span in which to make an impact! / Who can live forever with your tresses as crowns?",
    "literal": "I desire one life-span for effect, / who won the game of living with your locks on his head?",
    "poetic": "If only we had but one life-span to leave a mark. / Who could live forever with your tresses as crowns? ",
    "notes": ["The 'one life-span' is an allusion to the famous couplet by the 13th century Sufi poet Rumi: 'How I wish there were a single life-span in which to make an impact!' ('آه کو چاہيے اک عمر اثر ہوتے تک')\n\nThe wordplay is on the phrase 'zulf-e-sar' (tresses as crowns), which is a metaphor for beauty, and the game of living forever with them. Ghalib uses it to mean that no one can live forever in this world."
