    "literal": "Elevate your selfhood so much that before every decree, God asks His creations: 'Tell me what is your wish?'",
    "poetic": "Elevate your selfhood to such an extent that before every decree, God asks His creations: 'Tell me what is your wish?'",
    "notes": ["The wordplay in the first line is on the words 'خودی' (selfhood) and 'خدا' (God). 'خودی' means both selfhood and God. I have used the English word 'selfhood' to preserve the double meaning, although it is not a common word. In the last couplet, 'خدا' is also a pun on 'کھڑا' which means 'standing', indicating that before every decree, God stands in front of His creations and asks them what they wish for. I have used the word 'asks' to preserve this double meaning."
